From c221099f8a6170cf24bf70e3f94dbf0b74cb5023 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:07:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: every text of the player information fits as Kodi
 measures it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The texts of the player information were measured with PIL, which kerns
and does not hint as Kodi does: Kodi adds the advance of each glyph as
FreeType gives it with light hinting, thinned for a "lighten" font
(GUIFontTTF), and cuts with an ellipsis what is wider than its label. In
Kodi itself (QEMU), two texts that PIL said fit 280 px were cut and two
that PIL said were cut were shown whole; the battery's skin_check.py,
which measures as Kodi does, was right in all four. With it, and with
the widest values that the code gives, 18 labels were cut and three
columns held fewer rows than they can show.

Now, keeping the design of the panel:
- texts said in fewer words: the adaptation of HDR10 ("Yes: brighter
  than the display", "Sí: brilla más que la pantalla"), the depth set in
  the settings ("8-bit RGB setting"), the depth that the link limits
  ("all the link carries"), the depth of Dolby Vision ("8 bits: Dolby
  Vision carries 12 bits in them"), the signal of native Dolby Vision
  ("RGB 8 bits, no dithering"), L5 sent in Spanish ("con lo dibujado");
- rows whose name is short give their value the room (the mode, HDR10+
  average / 99 %, the L2 trims, L5 sent, the layout and the channels of
  the sound, Atmos, the last 10 s), the subtitle decoder in the smaller
  font;
- value labels that only an RPU with many blocks, many passes of the GPU
  or a backend's device name make wider than their row scroll (Kodi
  moves them only then): the metadata and the blocks sent, the GPU by
  pass, the device of live TV; and the colour of the film on the video
  page, one line that scrolls, so that the column holds its 18 rows;
- the signal of native Dolby Vision on one row, and the left column of
  the Dolby Vision page down to the strip (456 px), which holds its 11
  rows; the sound sent as, in three lines where es_mx needs them;
- the strip of the overview: the GPU says its temperature alone where
  its use is not known (HadesStripGpuVar; the system page says it), and
  the strip has the room of its frames dropped and skipped.

The row includes take "scroll" (HadesPanelRow, HadesPanelRowFlash) and
"height" and "valueheight" (HadesPanelRowText). system/hades is made
again by make-playerinfo.py.

Host test (outside the tree): skin_check.py (the battery's, with the
values that the window system publishes now, a value that an earlier one
of its variable covers left out, and a label that scrolls read in full):
28 failures before, none after; its 6 mutations and 2 more (the scroll
taken out, the covering value taken out) are caught.
